    "updated_at": "2024-05-02T16:43:25Z",
    "body": "> On Linux at least there's the `TIOCMIWAIT` operation for `ioctl` that accomplishes this.\r\n\r\nIf you spawn a thread exclusively for the purpose of waiting for signals. POSIX has frustratingly poor support for asynchronous I/O.",
