    "created_at": "2026-10-01T21:54:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T21:54:48Z",
    "body": "From a latency perspective, polling `getSignals()` every 100–500 ms imposes an artificial detection floor even on platforms that can report changes immediately.\n\nIt may be useful to specify `signalschange` as best-effort/event-driven: platforms with native notification use it directly; implementations without it may internally poll.\n\nThat keeps the cross-platform API consistent without requiring every OS backend to expose the same primitive.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
